-- title:
--   Reduction of χ(U_q) as Frobenius trace on inertia coinvariants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $N\ge 1$ and a finite set $S_0\subseteq\mathbb{N}$, and let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra away from $S_0$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$ and `heckeULin` for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$, $q\notin S_0$, and assume $\chi(U_q)$ is a unit. Let $k$ be a field, $\psi:k\to\operatorname{ResidueField}\mathcal{O}'$ a ring homomorphism and $\bar\rho$ a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a multiplicative action of $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite subextension pointwise, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$). Suppose there is a finite set $S$ such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ pushed along $\psi$ equals $X^2-\overline{\chi(T_\ell)}X+\ell$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring with $q$ a nonunit, suppose some element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ acts nontrivially, let $\sigma$ be a Frobenius at $q$ for $P$, and let $E$ be a $k$-endomorphism of $V/\sum_{\tau\in I_P}\operatorname{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ on classes. Then $\psi(\operatorname{tr}_k E)$ equals the residue of $\chi(U_q)$.
--
--   This is the $U_q$ part of the local description of the Hecke eigensystem at primes dividing the level exactly once, as in Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, Lemma 4.6: for a $p$-adic eigensystem with $\chi(U_q)$ a unit whose residual representation is $\bar\rho$ and is ramified at $q$, the reduction of the $U_q$-eigenvalue is the trace of Frobenius on the inertia coinvariants of $\bar\rho$. It is used in identifying the maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra attached to $\bar\rho$ and in the construction of ring homomorphisms from Hecke algebras with prescribed residual characteristic polynomials.
